                "cards": [
                  {
                    "id": "ceea22",
                    "text": "Nearly every teen already buckles up on every trip, so reminders add little value."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "cbc56f",
                    "text": "Belts only help when a vehicle is going faster than highway speed in a crash."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "c37aef",
                    "text": "Crash forces do not depend on who is riding, and male youth die from unintentional injuries at higher rates."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "c57278",
                    "text": "For front-seat riders, belts cut fatal-injury risk by about 60% in SUVs, trucks and vans."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "cb9b61",
                    "text": "Airbags are built to work together with seat belts, not to replace them."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "cffb7c",
                    "text": "Other drivers can cause a crash, and a belt protects you from mistakes your own skill cannot control."
                  }
                ],
                "targets": [
